  "stac_version": "1.1.0",
  "description": "WIMD is currently made up of eight separate domains (or types) of deprivation. Each domain is compiled from a range of different indicators (listed below). More details on the indicators can be found in our WIMD 2019 Technical Report .\n\nThe Index is constructed from a weighted sum of the deprivation score for each domain. The weights reflect the importance of the domain as an aspect of deprivation, and the quality of the indicators available for that domain.\n\nThe domains and their weights for WIMD 2019 are:\n\n\u2022 Income 22%\n\n\u2022 Employment 22%\n\n\u2022 Health 15%\n\n\u2022 Education 14%\n\n\u2022 Access to services 10%\n\n\u2022 Housing 7%\n\n\u2022 Community safety 5%\n\n\u2022 Physical environment 5%\n\nTo access all the individual spatial layers for the domains (types) of deprivation please click here .",
